  "details": "The chatbox notification sound plays at full volume upon hearing it for the first time when entering a world.\n\n**Steps to reproduce:**\n\n1. Enable chatbox notification sound\n\n2. Join a new instance\n\n3. Have someone send a chatbox message from very far away\n\n4. Have them send a second chatbox message\n\n**Actual result:**\n\nThe *first* chatbox sound will play at full volume as if next to your ear despite being far away, the *second* will play at a normal volume (Or be quiet depending on how far away they are)\n\n**Expected result:**\n\n*Both* chatbox sounds play at the appropriate volume according to the distance from the player\n\n**Notes:**\n\n- As far as I understand, this only happens the first time a message is sent from a specific user in an instance. Afterwards, any other chatbox pings from that user are played correctly. If a different user sends a message, the sound then plays incorrectly. *(EDITED)*\n\n- This has been happening for a very long time but I've listed the build number as 1347 because it's still an issue on the latest build as of writing this.",
